- Maintain a timer that resets on each detected event.
- On timeout (1440 min), trigger session cleanup and redirect to login.

#### 📦 Implementation Snippet:
```js
class InactivityMonitor {
  constructor(timeoutMinutes = 1440, onExpire) {
    this.timeoutMs = timeoutMinutes * 60 * 1000;
    this.timer = null;
    this.onExpire = onExpire;
    this.init();
  }

  reset() {
    if (this.timer) clearTimeout(this.timer);
    this.timer = setTimeout(() => {
      this.onExpire();
    }, this.timeoutMs);
  }

  init() {
    ACTIVITY_EVENTS.forEach(event =>
      document.addEventListener(event, () => this.reset(), { passive: true })
    );
    this.reset(); // Start initial countdown
  }

  stop() {
    if (this.timer) clearTimeout(this.timer);
  }
}
```

> ⚠️ This logic will be initialized post-login and destroyed on logout or expiry.

